# =============================================================================
#  §42 (Phase 3). What must never enter the image.
#
#  Two separate reasons, and both matter:
#    1. SECRETS. A file copied into a layer stays in that layer even if a
#       later layer deletes it. Anyone who can pull the image can read it.
#    2. REPRODUCIBILITY. Local output/, __pycache__ and venvs are
#       machine-specific. Including them makes two builds of the same tag
#       produce different images, which defeats the entire point of §42.
# =============================================================================

# ── Secrets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.template
.tokens/
tokens/
*.pem
*.p12
*.key
*.pickle
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# ── Local runtime data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
output/
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sql
!migrations/*.sql
*.sql.gz
*.postgres-backup-*

# ── Build and editor noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
node_modules/
venv/
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store

# ── Git: the .git directory is large and the image does not need history ────
# storage/version.py checks TP_VERSION before it shells out to `git describe`,
# and docker-compose.yml sets TP_VERSION on every service - so rows written
# from a container are stamped with the image tag, which is a stronger
# provenance claim than a describe of a detached checkout would be.
.git/
.github/

# ── Documentation and one-off artefacts ─────────────────────────────────────
*.docx
docs/releases/
BUILD_FROM_SCRATCH_GUIDE.md
